 -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $1$ pivot column (or alternatively, it has exactly $1$ non-zero row). \n\nTherefore, \n$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\\})=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
